L000483	
L000484	\textit{Conclusion}---We presented the first application of Flow Matching
L000485	to the problem of high-dimensional phase-space sampling in high-energy physics.
L000486	Our approach jointly remaps the input random numbers used to select continuous kinematic variables and discrete helicity configurations,
L000487	enabling more accurate and efficient sampling of complex final states.
L000488	A simple, file-based interface implemented in \Pepper, built around the \textsc{LHEH5} format, both facilitates the external optimization,
L000489	and the utilization of our results for further downstream simulation steps
L000490	using established event generation frameworks
L000491	such as \textsc{Sherpa} and \textsc{Pythia}.
L000492	Focusing on two challenging benchmark processes,
L000493	lepton-pair and top--antitop pair production with up to five and four associated jets, respectively,
L000494	we demonstrated unweighting efficiency improvements of up to 184$\times$ and 25$\times$ over \textsc{Vegas} baseline results.
L000495	We further showed that a significant fraction of the efficiency gains achieved with Flow-Matching--based ODE Flows
L000496	can be transferred effectively to fast Coupling-Layer--based Flows using the
L000497	RegFlow method, yielding event generation walltime reductions of around a factor of ten
L000498	at the highest jet numbers studied.
L000499	This shows that the efficiency of Coupling-Layer--based Flows
L000500	can be substantially improved by effectively using a Matching Flow objective
L000501	instead of the minimum likelihood objective otherwise used to train them in this and previous studies.
L000502	We further expect that ODE Flows themselves will become
L000503	significantly faster as these architectures mature and more efficient
L000504	implementations are developed.
L000505	
L000506	While our study concentrated on one dominant partonic channel for each process,
L000507	full simulations will require all contributing channels.
L000508	Future work will extend the method to a single, conditional model that simultaneously
L000509	learns across multiple partonic channels and jet multiplicities, leveraging inter-channel correlations for further gains in sampling efficiency.
L000510	The sampling method improved in this way
L000511	will be made available as part of a future public \Pepper\ release,
L000512	contributing to a successful High-Luminosity LHC
L000513	and future collider physics programs.\\[0.5em]
